@startuml architecture
title Current architecture — composition and main dependencies
top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Composition and UI" {
  component "main.py\nComposition Root" as Main
  component "CLI" as CLI
}

package Application {
  component "MenuOrchestrator" as MenuApp
  component "ShoppingListOrchestrator" as ShoppingApp
  component "CRUD services" as CRUD
  interface "UnitOfWork" as UoW
}

package Domain {
  component "MealBlockGenerator" as BlockGen
  component "MenuPlanner / MenuEditor" as Planning
  component "AvailableRecipeList" as Available
  component "RecipeExclusions" as CombinedEx
  component "UserExclusions" as UserEx
  component "SystemExclusions" as SystemEx
  component "ShoppingListGenerator" as ShoppingGen
  interface "Repository ports\nRecipeRepository\nIngredientRepository\nRecipeIngredientRepository" as Ports
}

package Infrastructure {
  component "SQL repositories" as SqlRepos
  component "SqlUnitOfWork" as SqlUoW
  database PostgreSQL as DB
}

Main ..> CLI : injects application services
Main ..> MenuApp : constructs and wires
Main ..> ShoppingApp
Main ..> CRUD

CLI --> MenuApp
CLI --> ShoppingApp
CLI --> CRUD
CLI --> UserEx : adds / removes exclusions
MenuApp --> BlockGen
MenuApp --> Planning
MenuApp --> SystemEx : clears and synchronizes
ShoppingApp --> ShoppingGen
CRUD --> UoW

BlockGen --> Available
Available --> CombinedEx : checks exclusions
CombinedEx --> UserEx
CombinedEx --> SystemEx
Available --> Ports : recipes
ShoppingGen --> Ports : recipe ingredients

SqlUoW ..|> UoW
SqlUoW --> SqlRepos : shared connection per CRUD operation
SqlRepos ..|> Ports
SqlRepos --> DB

note right of Main
The Composition Root also creates the domain services,
exclusion instances, and SQL repositories, then wires
them into the application services passed to the CLI.
The wiring arrows shown here are intentionally selective.
end note

note bottom of SqlRepos
Menu generation and shopping-list calculation use
SQL repositories on a connection kept open during
the CLI session. CRUD services create one
SqlUnitOfWork and connection per operation.
This is the current implementation, not a design rule.
end note
@enduml
